<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The Bank is widely expected to announce it=
s first increase in UK interest rates in more than three years. A quarter-p=
oint rise would take the Bank rate up to 4% from 3.75%.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">With inflation rising faster than the Bank=
=E2=80=99s target, most of its policymakers are expected to decide now is t=
he moment to tighten monetary policy. This, they may hope, would dampen the=
 risk that high energy costs spill over and push up the cost of other goods=
 and services.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The Bank has not increased borrowing costs=
 since August 2023, when the Bank rate hit 5.25%.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">It will also be playing =E2=80=9Ccatchup=
=E2=80=9D with other central banks =E2=80=93 rates have already risen in th=
e US, Japan, the eurozone, Australia and Canada this year.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Deutsche Bank analysts predict the Bank of=
 England=E2=80=99s monetary policy committee will split 6-3 in today=E2=80=
=99s vote, with a majority voting for a rate increase to 4%.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The committee is split between hawks (who =
want higher rates to fight inflation) and doves (who fear higher rates will=
 hurt economic growth).</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Deutsche Bank also predicts the Bank=E2=80=
=99s latest economic forecasts will show inflation rising as high as 4.25% =
by the first quarter of 2027, along with an upgrade to the 2026 growth fore=
cast to 1.4%.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The Bank of England will be reassured to s=
ee that the oil price has tumbled this week.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Brent crude fell through the $100 a barrel=
 mark yesterday, hitting its lowest level in two months, and this morning i=
s trading at about $95 a barrel.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Traders appear to be concluding that Donal=
d Trump may try to de-escalate the Middle East conflict after his Republica=
n party were given <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c=
